# This site's own data: what its pages say about themselves. Hugo reads
# every key here as site.Params.<name> -- the file's name is what makes
# them params -- and the theme renders from those: the marks in the
# masthead and where they point, the banner above the header, the
# newsletter band, the line under every page, the picture a share of a
# coverless page carries. It is the one file to edit to rename this
# site's own furniture, and the exporter fills it from the archive's
# site/site.json.
#
# Its address, its name and its language are hugo.toml beside this
# file, Hugo taking those at the root of its configuration; the
# landing page's blurb is content/_index.md; the names tags and
# authors are shown under are data/tags.json and data/authornames.json.
$params
